SDUSD::upgradeToAndCall
├── when called directly on an implementation
│   └── it should revert with UUPSUnauthorizedCallContext
├── when called through the proxy by a non-owner
│   ├── when the new implementation is UUPS compatible
│   │   └── it should revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount
│   └── when the new implementation is not UUPS compatible
│       └── it should revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount before checking compatibility
└── when called through the proxy by the owner
    ├── when the new implementation is not UUPS compatible
    │   └── it should revert
    └── when the new implementation is UUPS compatible
        ├── it should update the proxy implementation
        ├── it should emit Upgraded
        ├── it should preserve ownership and pending ownership
        ├── it should preserve pauser permissions and pause state
        ├── it should preserve the asset, seed shares, rewarder, and next reward duration
        ├── it should preserve total supply, accounted assets, and share balances
        ├── it should preserve the active reward amount and period timestamps
        ├── it should preserve locked rewards, total assets, and the exchange rate at the upgrade timestamp
        ├── it should continue releasing the active reward over its original duration
        └── when initialization calldata is provided
            └── it should delegatecall the new implementation with the provided calldata
